---
import AppLandingPage from '../../components/AppLandingPage.astro';
import { LEARNING_APPS } from '../../data/apps';
import { priceText } from '../../data/stores';

// Every app covering at least one of the three radio certificates.
const apps = LEARNING_APPS.filter(app =>
  app.licenses.some(l => l === 'ubi' || l === 'src' || l === 'lrc')
);

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Which app is best for the radio certificate?',
    a: 'The field is smaller than for the boating licence: five apps cover the radio certificates. Bootspruefung.de adds sample radio messages, SBF-Fragen from publisher Delius Klasing uses a spaced-repetition box, Bootsprüfung covers UBI, SRC and LRC together with SBF and the Lake Constance licence, Bootsschule1 offers UBI and SRC as part of its courses, and Boatpass bundles the three radio catalogues with SBF See and Binnen in one app. The free Wimmer apps, the Goritz apps and Sailbyte cover no radio certificates.',
  },
  {
    q: 'UBI, SRC or LRC – which certificate do I need?',
    a: 'UBI covers VHF radio on German inland waterways, SRC covers VHF marine radio in coastal waters, and LRC covers worldwide maritime radio including satellite communication. They are not mutually creditable, but holders of a maritime certificate get a shortened UBI exam.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I practise the practical radio exam with an app?',
    a: 'No. All three certificates include a practical part: operating the equipment, setting ATIS, and distress, urgency and safety messages. An app prepares the theory and familiarises you with the procedures – speaking on the radio has to be practised.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a free radio certificate app?',
    a: 'With Bootspruefung.de all official exam questions – including UBI, SRC and LRC – are free to use; theory texts, sample radio messages and full offline use sit in the Pro version. SBF-Fragen and Boatpass show a subset for free, with the full catalogues paid. A permanently and completely free radio app, like the Wimmer apps for the boating licence, does not exist.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How many questions does the UBI exam have?',
    a: 'The official UBI catalogue holds 130 questions. The exam paper contains 22 multiple-choice questions in 60 minutes, passed from 17 correct answers, plus the practical part.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are the radio apps available for iPhone?',
    a: 'Yes. All five apps – Bootspruefung.de, Bootsprüfung, Bootsschule1, SBF-Fragen and, since October 2026, Boatpass – are available for Android and iOS.',
  },
];

const relatedLinks = [
  { href: '/en/ubi/', label: 'UBI – VHF radio certificate for inland waters' },
  { href: '/en/src/', label: 'SRC – Short Range Certificate' },
  { href: '/en/lrc/', label: 'LRC – Long Range Certificate' },
  { href: '/en/sbf-app/', label: 'All boating licence apps compared' },
  { href: '/en/blog/ubi-vs-src-radio-license/', label: 'UBI or SRC – which radio certificate do you need?' },
  { href: '/en/faq/', label: 'Frequently asked questions about German boating licences' },
];
---

<AppLandingPage
  lang="en"
  title="Radio certificate app: learn UBI, SRC and LRC"
  description="Looking for a radio certificate app for UBI, SRC or LRC? We compare question catalogues, prices and platforms – from Bootspruefung.de to Boatpass."
  altUrl="https://boatpass.de/funkschein-app/"
  path="/radio-certificate-app/"
  breadcrumbName="Radio certificate apps compared"
  badge="UBI · SRC · LRC"
  h1="Radio certificate apps compared"
  heroIntro="For the radio certificates the choice is far smaller than for the boating licence – five apps cover UBI, SRC or LRC at all. Here they are side by side."
  answer="Five learning apps cover at least one of the German radio certificates UBI, SRC and LRC: Bootspruefung.de with free official questions and sample radio messages in its Pro version, SBF-Fragen from publisher Delius Klasing with a spaced-repetition box, Bootsprüfung as the newest provider with all three certificates, Bootsschule1 with UBI and SRC as part of a course, and Boatpass, which bundles all three radio catalogues with SBF See and Binnen in one app."
  apps={apps}
  tableCaption="Every app covering at least one of the radio certificates UBI, SRC or LRC – sorted alphabetically."
  androidHeading="Radio certificate app for Android"
  androidParagraphs={[
    'All five apps are on Google Play. The difference lies less in the question catalogue – that is official and identical everywhere – than in what surrounds it: <strong>Bootspruefung.de</strong> supplies sample radio messages and theory texts in its Pro version, while <strong>SBF-Fragen</strong> relies on a spaced-repetition box with exam simulation on original papers.',
    'The popular free apps by Matthias Wimmer cover <strong>no radio certificates</strong>, and neither do the Goritz apps or Sailbyte. <strong>Bootsprüfung</strong> is new to the market and covers all three certificates, while <strong>Bootsschule1</strong> offers UBI and SRC only as part of its paid courses.',
    'With Boatpass the radio modules cost ' + priceText('ubi', 'en') + ' one-off (UBI and SRC) and ' + priceText('lrc', 'en') + ' (LRC) – no subscription, permanent access.',
  ]}
  iosHeading="Radio certificate app for iPhone and iPad"
  iosParagraphs={[
    'On iOS all five compared apps are available. <strong>Bootspruefung.de</strong>, <strong>SBF-Fragen</strong>, <strong>Bootsprüfung</strong> and <strong>Boatpass</strong> cover UBI, SRC and LRC, <strong>Bootsschule1</strong> covers UBI and SRC.',
    '<strong>Boatpass has been on the App Store since October 2026</strong>. Both stores also offer a radio bundle for all three certificates. A purchase only applies to the store you bought in, so an Android purchase does not unlock anything on iPhone.',
  ]}
  strengths={[
    'UBI, SRC and LRC in the same app as SBF See and SBF Binnen',
    'Complete official catalogues, including 130 UBI questions',
    'Exam simulation with pass mark and time limit',
    'Mistake training for the classic stumbling blocks in distress procedures',
    'One-off purchase per radio module, also as a radio bundle on the App Store – no subscription',
    'Study offline – works without an internet connection',
  ]}
  limitations={[
    'No FKN pyrotechnics certificate and no Lake Constance licence',
    'Purchases apply per store – no transfer between Android and iPhone',
    'No audio sample radio messages – the practical exam is practised on the equipment',
    'Far fewer ratings than Bootspruefung.de and SBF-Fragen',
    'Does not replace the practical part of the radio exam',
  ]}
  faqs={faqs}
  relatedLinks={relatedLinks}
>
  <section slot="after-table" style="margin-bottom:48px;">
    <h2 class="content-section-title" style="margin-bottom:16px;">Theory and practice: what a radio app can do</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:#4B5563; line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:12px;">
      Every radio certificate has two parts. The theory is a multiple-choice paper from the official catalogue – exactly what the apps are built for. In the practical part you operate a radio set, send a DSC alert and speak distress, urgency and safety messages in a fixed format. No app replaces that.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:#4B5563; line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:12px;">
      What apps can contribute to the practical part is limited: <strong>Bootspruefung.de</strong> offers sample radio messages to read through, while the other apps focus on the theory. For the practical part you need a course with a training set or a radio simulator. Do not underestimate it: in the exam you have to know the fixed sequence of a distress message without notes.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:#4B5563; line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:12px;">
      For the UBI, a new official question catalogue has applied since 1 October 2026. Make sure your app already includes it; what has changed is explained in the article <a href="/en/blog/ubi-question-catalog-2026/" style="color:#3366FF; text-decoration:underline;">UBI question catalogue 2026</a>. Which certificate you need is covered on the pages for <a href="/en/ubi/" style="color:#3366FF; text-decoration:underline;">UBI</a>, <a href="/en/src/" style="color:#3366FF; text-decoration:underline;">SRC</a> and <a href="/en/lrc/" style="color:#3366FF; text-decoration:underline;">LRC</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</AppLandingPage>
